- OBSERVATION (RESOLVED — see above): per-refresh `auth.refresh` auditing (owner-mandated in R16) writes one row per refresh per session. At §2.4 scale that is roughly **800k–900k audit rows/year**, against §2.4's stated envelope of **~100k/year and a 1M total design ceiling** — i.e. the envelope is reached within about a year. Nothing is under-specified for implementation, so this is recorded rather than blocking. Two related choices the Owner may want to make together: whether `auth.*` lifecycle rows fall under TD-8's **12-month login-audit retention** or its indefinite retention (TD-8 says "Login audits retain 12 months; all other audit rows retained indefinitely" without classifying the new rows), and whether §2.4's audit estimate should be revised.
